0011 — an `animate-<name>` naming nothing is a build error listing the
declared names, instead of dropping the whole class literal silently.

Rebased onto 66caf4e5 (2026-10-22). Main's `unknownUtilities` (#557) asks
`parseAnimation` whether a token is a utility, and this patch's
`parseAnimation` defers an unknown name instead of refusing it. Through
main's accumulator, which has no deferral arrays, the deferral threw, the
throw was caught as "a loud rule", and a misspelt animation was no longer
reported in a class literal that failed on another token first.
`unknownUtilities` now passes a whole accumulator and counts a deferred
name or loop as unknown. Main's `animate-loop-[4x]` assertion is red
without that; one more pins a misspelt name beside another bad token.

